  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A granny square join blanket is made from 42 classic four-round squares, each 15 cm across, joined edge to edge as you crochet the final round of each new square. The finished piece is 90 x 105 cm, which drapes a standard single bed to the pillow line."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jayg"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "join-as-you-go"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " method means no sewing at the end: when you reach a corner or side chain on the final round, you slip stitch into the matching point on the neighbouring square instead of chaining. Work all squares in the same colour for a clean grid look, or change colour square by square for a patchwork effect. Yardage for the solid version is 400 g DK cotton on a 4 mm hook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "400 g total (one or more colours)"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "Stitch markers",
              "qty": "4"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One four-round granny square = 15 x 15 cm with a 4 mm hook in DK cotton, unblocked. Make one test square and measure across the centre from edge to edge. If it measures more than 15 cm, go down one hook size; if less, go up. At 15 cm per square, 6 across x 7 down gives 90 x 105 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "MR"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ": magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "sl st: slip stitch (closing rounds and JAYG joins)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tr (UK) / dc (US): treble"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "gr-cl: granny cluster, 3 tr into the same "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "chain-space"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "chain space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Single square, four rounds"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1: Ch 3 (counts as 1 tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. Ch 2. *3 tr into the ring, ch 2*. Repeat 3 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3 to close. Pull ring closed. (4 gr-cl, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2: Sl st across to first ch-2 corner space. Ch 3. Work (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into same corner space. *Ch 1. Work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into next corner space*. Repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1. Sl st to close. (8 gr-cl, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 sides.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3: Sl st to corner. Ch 3. Work (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner. *Ch 1. Work 3 tr into ch-1 side space. Ch 1. Work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into next corner*. Repeat 3 more times ending with ch 1. Sl st to close. (12 gr-cl, 4 corners, 8 sides.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4: Work as Round 3, adding one more ch-1 and 3-tr cluster on each side. (16 gr-cl, 4 corners, 12 sides.) Fasten off leaving a tail for weaving."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join-as-you-go on Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On the final square in a row or when placing a square adjacent to a completed square, replace each joining ch-2 corner with \"ch 1, sl st into matching corner space of adjacent square, ch 1\", and replace each joining ch-1 side with \"sl st into matching side space of adjacent square\". This creates a flat, invisible join."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Working order"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the first 6 squares (one full row) individually, then join each subsequent square on Round 4 to its left-hand neighbour. When starting a new row, join each new square to the square above as well as to the left. Work 7 rows of 6 squares each."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After joining, work one round of dc (UK) around the entire blanket border: 1 dc into each stitch, 1 dc into each ch-1 side space, 2 dc into each ch-2 corner, and 1 dc into each join point. This smooths the outer edge and ties the squares into one fabric."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with the tapestry needle to secure all tails. Block: wet-block the cotton by submerging in cool water, squeezing out excess, and pinning flat to the stated dimensions. Allow to dry completely before unpinning."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees, gentle cycle. Reshape while damp and dry flat. DK cotton does not tumble dry well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Try the granny hexagon blanket next, or the c2c blanket for a diagonal take on the same stitch."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}